cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use vwatch or its eval harness, please cite it as below."
title: "vwatch: an agent toolkit that watches video like a person"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: kashaf12
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-23
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kashaf12/vwatch"
url: "https://github.com/kashaf12/vwatch"
abstract: >-
  vwatch is an agent toolkit for video understanding with large language models.
  Instead of sampling frames uniformly, it plans from the question, skims at low
  resolution while the model predicts what should happen next, uses model-free
  signal hints, and spends its token budget on dense seeks, crops and listens at
  the surprising moments. It ships with an eval harness that compares this against
  uniform frame sampling, ablations, and existing Claude Code video tools at a
  matched evidence-token budget.
keywords:
  - video understanding
  - multimodal agents
  - large language models
  - evaluation
  - frame sampling
